INSERT OR IGNORE INTO problems (slug, title, body, difficulty, tags, starter, cases, solution, source_url, status, created_by) VALUES ('pair-sums', 'Pair sums', 'In the math club''s card game, every card has an integer on it, and some are negative. A pair of cards scores if their two numbers add up to exactly K. How many different pairs of cards score?

Two pairs are different if they use a different two cards, even when the numbers are the same.

## Input

The first line has N and K. The second line has N integers: the numbers on the cards.

## Output

Print the number of pairs of positions i < j where card i plus card j equals K.

## Constraints

- 2 ≤ N ≤ 2,000
- -1,000,000 ≤ each card ≤ 1,000,000
- -2,000,000 ≤ K ≤ 2,000,000

## Sample input

```
6 4
2 2 2 1 3 0
```

## Sample output

```
